#!/usr/bin/python3.12 -I
"""Linux execution side of the resident in-place upgrade (DESIGN, task 018da927, spec B3). FROZEN: installed by
root as /opt/clued-independent-ci/upgrade-v1/bin/clued-ci-upgrade-linux and changed only by a full reinstall;
every rollback is executed by this same frozen code.

  clued-ci-upgrade-linux version-facts
  clued-ci-upgrade-linux stage    --op UUID --package SHA256 --generation N --linux-manifest SHA256
  clued-ci-upgrade-linux switch   --op UUID --from N --to M --linux-manifest SHA256
  clued-ci-upgrade-linux rollback --op UUID --from M --to N        (M = the generation given up, N = the one restored)
  clued-ci-upgrade-linux verify   --generation N
  clued-ci-upgrade-linux retain   --op UUID --keep K [--generation N]   (mailbox kind linux-upgrade-retain {keep}; K 2..10)
  clued-ci-upgrade-linux adopt    --generation 1 --package SHA256  (root, from install-resident-linux.sh: first install and
                                                                    every full reinstall, after the uninstall archived the old state)

One JSON object on one stdout line; exit 0 only on success. Root on Linux only.

Layout (spec A6): the active paths never change (loadQualifiedPolicyV2 refuses links):
  /opt/clued-independent-ci/{source-v2,resident-v1}, /etc/clued-independent-ci/{roles-v3,formal-source-manifest-v2.json},
  /etc/systemd/system/clued-ci-{worker,wsprep,archive}@.service
  staging   /opt/clued-independent-ci/.next-<opId>/{package/, source-v2, resident-v1, roles-work/, roles-v3,
            formal-source-manifest-v2.json, units/}
  parked    /opt/clued-independent-ci/generations/g<N>/<item>     (what generation N had live before it was replaced)
  archive   /opt/clued-independent-ci/archive/                     (retention and leftovers: renamed, never deleted)
  state     /var/lib/clued-independent-ci/resident/upgrade/{current.json, g<N>.json}

Every item is identified by (st_dev, st_ino), which a rename keeps, so a re-run re-observes where each item is:
"the old one still live / parked under generations / the new one live" (spec A4). g<N>.json is the commit point of
`stage` (written create-only, last); current.json (whole-file replace) is the commit point of switch and rollback.
Every move is a rename without replace: the destination is checked absent and renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE) is used
where libc and the file system offer it; otherwise (ENOSYS/EINVAL, or a libc without renameat2) a checked
os.rename is used and the result reports renameMode "checked-rename" (no other writer exists under quiescence and
the single-instance lock).

roles-v3 derivation: the installed policy and the installed signed v2 payload are copied, and ONLY the Source
binding fields of qualification-v2.mjs:46-56 change (sourceManifestSha256, entrySha256, qualificationSha256,
workerSha256, proofSha256, jobSha256, sourceAcceptanceRef); host facts (image, key, runtime, host acceptance,
executables) are carried. The derived policy file bytes (canonical JSON + "\\n") must hash to the package's
linux.sourceV2.rolesDerivedSha256[role]; the installed signer signs them against the installed v2 qualification.
"""
import ctypes
import datetime
